    "reason": "The assertion treats a probabilistic correlation as a deterministic guarantee. While lower precision generally reduces storage, this is contingent on the data type mapping (e.g., float32 to int8 saves space, but float16 to int4 might not if overhead increases) and compression schemes. Furthermore, 'smaller' is relative; without defining the baseline or accounting for metadata overhead in specific ",
